    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.sessions\n\n### Description\n\nHello, I've been trying to combine `mini.sessions` with Git worktrees.\n\nI'm trying to build a workflow where each worktree has a dedicated session file (e.g. `Session.vim`) and switching between worktrees would save/load a local session to persist active buffers.\n\nI've stumbled upon a blocker on `mini.sessions` - the module won't allow to load a session file which doesn't present in `MiniSessions.detected` list.\n\nI tried different workarounds to solve this problem, they're fragile and end up corrupting sessions, buffers, etc:\n\n```lua\n-- Persist current session\n    sessions.write(nil, {\n      verbose = false,\n    })\n\n-- Prevent mini writing to a previous worktree session\n    sessions.detected[vim.v.this_session] = nil\n    vim.v.this_session = ''\n\n-- I had a problem of new buffers being present in a new session\n    for _, buf in ipairs(vim.api.nvim_list_bufs()) do\n      vim.api.nvim_buf_delete(buf, { force = true })\n    end\n\n-- cd and load new session\n      vim.api.nvim_set_current_dir(path)\n      sessions.read(M.session_file, { force = true, verbose = false })\n```\n\nCan `mini.sessions` introduce a manual way of switching local sessions that don't require brittle hack and mutating plugin's internal state.\n\nIdeally, I would like to have a dedicated `read_dir_session` method that only operates on local sessions, without `detected` list being used:\n\n```\n--- @class ReadDirSessionOpts\n--- @member force boolean|nil Whether to delete unsaved buffers\n--- @member create_session boolean|nil Create a local session at destination dir if not exist.\n\n--- Open a local session located at a different directory.\n--- @param path string Path to a target directory\n--- @param opts ReadDirSessionOpts|nil Options\nMiniSessions.read_dir_session = function(path, opts)\n```\n\nThe `opts.create_session` option can be used for newly created worktrees which don't yet have a session.",
