        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\n\nI don't think 'mini.sessions' is the right tool for the problem described. Its most value comes from persistent global sessions that can be sourced from any working directory. Support for local sessions is present only as they were/are pretty popular (although I would not use them).\n\nThe 'mini.sessions' module is basically a wrapper around [`:mksession` command](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/402ee6c6ec8ea44b22330446c8fb4e615fd3953e/doc/mini-sessions.txt#L25-L28). My suggestion for this particular use case would be to\n- Explicitly use `:mksession! Session.vim` to write current session in the current working directory.\n- `:cd new-worktree`\n- `:source Session.vim` for the local session in the new worktree.\n\nDoes this solve your initial workflow problem?",
