        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "@echasnovski thanks for a quick reply!\n\nI have a mixed workflow (local sessions for worktrees and global sessions for the rest of repos), so I can't just stop using this great plugin\n\nI was thinking about attacking the problem manually, but I really value that `mini.sessions` handles session autosave, buffer cleanups during session transitions, unsaved buffers guards and other stuff.\n\nIn addition to that, as I still would like to use mini.sessions for non-worktree repos, the manual approach will conflict with the plugin.\n\nIf I open nvim in a worktree with local session - I would still need to make the plugin to forget about it during transition.\n\nI can disable session file name in the plugin config, but then I will loose mini's quality of live features.",
