            "body": "> [@echasnovski](https://github.com/echasnovski) would you be interested in this feature if I'll make a PR?\n\nI am still not quite sure what is the workflow problem with 'mini.sessions'. Why is `:cd new-worktree` followed by `:lua MiniSessions.read('Session.vim')` not enough? The quick test shows that this works as expected:\n- Create `worktree-1/file-1` file, `:cd worktree-1`, `:lua MiniSessions.write('Session.vim')`.\n- Wipeout buffer for `file-a`, create `worktree-2/file-2` file, `:cd ../worktree-1`, `:lua MiniSessions.write('Session.vim')`. There are now two local session files: `worktree-1/Session.vim` and `worktree-2/Session.vim`.\n- Doing `:cd ../worktree-1` to go back to previous worktree and executing `:lua MiniSessions.read('Session.vim')` loads the local session for `worktree-1`.",
